solution_stdout:
[solution] 'cni0' already exists but is stuck on the WRONG subnet
[solution] (left over from an earlier, unrelated pod attachment). The
[solution] bridge CNI plugin refuses to just bolt a second, conflicting
[solution] address onto an existing bridge -- exactly like the real bug
[solution] report's own accepted answer describes. A Linux bridge can
[solution] only sanely serve one subnet at a time, and the CORRECT fix
[solution] is to reset it so it gets recreated fresh for the actual
[solution] intended subnet -- not to change netconf.json to match
[solution] whatever subnet happens to already be there.
  -> OK ('cni0' removed)
[solution] attaching the pod network namespace via the real bridge +
[solution] host-local CNI plugins -- the same CNI_COMMAND=ADD protocol
[solution] CRI-O/kubelet use -- against the CURRENT, correct netconf...
[solution] CNI ADD result:
